{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stage gate stage gate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md","fileName":"Stage Gate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stage Gate","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Production Planning and Milestones]] [[Software Engineering]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Production Planning and Milestones","Software Engineering","Design-Build-Test Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stage gate stage gate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md","fileName":"Stage Gate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stage Gate","heading":"Stage Gate","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A stage gate is a deliberate checkpoint at which a project is evaluated for viability, progress, risk, and continued investment. A concept may pass forward, return for significant revision, or be removed from active development.\n\nStage gates bound an otherwise open-ended [[Design-Build-Test Loop]]. They allow exploration while preventing iteration from becoming indefinite motion without progress, and they preserve rejected ideas for possible future use rather than forcing sunk-cost continuation.\n\nA gate can coexist with agile delivery when it evaluates demonstrated results, current risks, and updated forecasts. Treating the gate as approval of a frozen speculative plan instead suppresses the evidence that iteration was meant to produce.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Production Planning and Milestones","Software Engineering","Design-Build-Test Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"stage gate stage gate","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Stage Gate.md","fileName":"Stage Gate.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Stage Gate","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Production Planning and Milestones","Software Engineering","Design-Build-Test Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}